;; si's check's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a); arbace.scheme.check, judge; SCS3): the subject program's run
;; (bin/si check's, or bin/si check --aot's) judged by the subject's own judge against the reference program's expectation: a
;; suite's program against the reference's count of tests (:tests of test/scheme/si/programs.edn: a run that reports fewer tests
;; than it must, the own verdict's blind spot scheme-90 noted), si's own and Larceny's program against the reference's golden
;; output (SCS6 (b): Larceny's have golden outputs too), a benchmark against the reference's name (SCS8 (b)); the check fails when the judge finds no item (it passes what
;; differs) or when the reference has no expectation of that kind. No program or run of its own: two programs of
;; test/scheme/si/programs.edn, both passing, with other outputs; each control's programs are in both essential subsets. A control
;; whose subject was not selected (--only) or not run is left. No control is a program of the results, the classes or the counts.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "_control/enums-vs-lists" :subject "racket/enums" :reference "racket/lists"
  :why "the own report's count: enums' 26 tests against the 72 lists must report (a count item: a run cut short)"}
 {:id "_control/amb-vs-data" :subject "si/amb" :reference "si/data"
  :why "the golden output: amb's stdout against data's golden (a differs item)"}
 {:id "_control/run-benchmark-vs-exceptions" :subject "larceny/run-benchmark" :reference "larceny/exceptions"
  :why "Larceny's golden outputs (SCS6): run-benchmark's stdout against exceptions' golden (a differs item)"}
 {:id "_control/nboyer-vs-earley" :subject "larceny/nboyer" :reference "larceny/earley"
  :why "a benchmark's own result check (SCS8 (b)): nboyer's run against earley's name (a no-report item: run-benchmark never ran earley)"}
 {:id "_control/eval-library-vs-data" :subject "si/eval-library" :reference "si/data"
  :why "SCS30: eval-library's stdout (the compiled library's one instance seen by eval) against data's golden (a differs item)"}]
